| Data Structure | Load / Create Course Objects | Search for One Course | Print Courses in Order | Memory Use |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Vector | O(n) | O(n) | O(n log n) | O(n) |
| Hash Table | O(n) average, O(n²) worst case | O(1) average, O(n) worst case | O(n log n) | O(n) |
| Binary Search Tree | O(n log n) average, O(n²) worst case | O(log n) average, O(n) worst case | O(n) | O(n) |

Advantages and Disadvantages

The vector is the simplest structure to use. It is easy to add courses and loop through them. However, it does not search as quickly as the other options because it may need to check every course one at a time. It also has to be sorted before printing the course list in alphanumeric order.

The hash table is the fastest option for searching for a specific course on average. This makes it useful when the main goal is quick lookup. However, it does not naturally keep courses sorted, so extra work is needed to print the courses in alphanumeric order. Hash collisions can also make performance worse.

The binary search tree is useful because it supports both searching and sorted printing. An in-order traversal can print the courses in alphanumeric order without needing a separate sort. Searching is also efficient when the tree is balanced. A disadvantage is that if the tree becomes unbalanced, performance can become slower.

Recommendation

Based on the advisor’s requirements, I recommend using a binary search tree. ABCU needs the program to print all computer science courses in alphanumeric order and also search for a specific course to display its title and prerequisites. A binary search tree works well for both tasks because it can search efficiently and print courses in sorted order using an in-order traversal.

A hash table may be faster for searching one course, but it does not naturally keep courses sorted. A vector is simple, but searching is slower and sorting is required before printing. Since this program needs both sorted output and individual course lookup, the binary search tree is the best overall choice.
